      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1871 the Atchison, Topeka and Santa Fe Railway built a main line and a nearby station named Cedar Grove north of Cedar Point.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedar_Point%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The 1868 Cedar Point Mill, a flour mill, was partially restored in the early 21st century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cedar_Point%2C_Kansas",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Today Cedar Point is a semi‑ghost town with several remaining buildings and a historic flour mill.",
